A||||2||GT Bastard||Need Isuzu clutch info...||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-31-2000||02:07 AM||||Hey guys... Does anybody know the part # for the RAM HD clutch for the 5sp Isuzu? Not the Fiero store one, but the RAM PN#.  What other semi-heavy duty clutches exist for the ISUZU, and where's the best place to get them? thanks guys!||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||03-31-2000||12:05 PM||||GT Bastard,<P>I believe another post stated that you need the clutch for the transaxle you are using.<P>Well, that is sort of correct.  Actually the only thing that changes is the throwout bearing needs to be for the transaxle you are using.<P>I am using a CenterForce dual friction setup in my HO Quad 4 swap.  It is listed for a Beretta V6 with the Muncie 5 speed but it also fits the HO Quad 4 with either transaxle (Isuzu or Muncie).  The difference is what throwout bearing is used.<P>I have a transaxle from a 97 Sunfire 2.4 Twincam.  It is an Isuzu 5 speed that is real close to be exactly like the Fiero's Isuzu.  Close enough that I used the Fiero Isuzu's shift mechanism in place of the SunFire Isuzu's mechanism.  I only had to make one hole elongated to make it bolt on with all 4 bolts.  <P>The proof will be when I get the slave cylinder of this transaxle to work with the new master cylinder I had to buy (original one had the internal spring break!) AND I get the engine fired!  Until then, I just have assembled parts.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Paul<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||terryk||03-31-2000||04:52 PM||||Check the pressure plate clearance to the transaxle. One plate I used hit the inside of the Isuzu bellhousings. A bit of grinding in there solved. Makes a creep noise if you don't.<P>TK||||reg||1
